The writable constructions fail H because the paper provides their swap schedules explicitly. At the largest fitting Section 4 instance, the mechanical and compact routes both require 252 operations. Conversely, the paper’s genuinely NP-complete weighted-coloured spider construction requires at least 6,103,437,500 swaps even at its smallest stated regime, violating the certificate caps. The unrestricted inverse-scramble proposal is also polynomially solvable via the paper’s \(O(n^2)\) leaf-first algorithm. See the [full paper](https://arxiv.org/html/1903.06981v5).

